---The Amazon S3 destination where errors associated with the job creation request are saved.
---@class aws.iotsitewise.ErrorReportLocation
---@field bucket aws.iotsitewise.Bucket The name of the Amazon S3 bucket to which errors associated with the bulk import job are sent.
---@field prefix aws.iotsitewise.String Amazon S3 uses the prefix as a folder name to organize data in the bucket. Each Amazon S3 object has a key that is its unique identifier in the bucket. Each object in a bucket has exactly one key. The prefix must end with a forward slash (/). For more information, see Organizing objects using prefixes in the Amazon Simple Storage Service User Guide.

---Configuration for event detection enrichment on video time-series data.
---@class aws.iotsitewise.EventDetection
---@field datasetId aws.iotsitewise.ID The IoT SiteWise dataset ID containing the video time-series data to analyze. Query IoT SiteWise to discover available datasets in your workspace.
---@field timeSeriesId? aws.iotsitewise.TimeSeriesId Unique system identifier for the video time series to analyze. Specify either timeSeriesId or propertyAlias, but not both. Use this when you have the system-generated time series identifier from IoT SiteWise.
---@field propertyAlias? aws.iotsitewise.AssetPropertyAlias Human-readable alias for the video time series to analyze (e.g., /camera/warehouse/zone-a). Specify either propertyAlias or timeSeriesId, but not both. Use this when you have configured friendly aliases in IoT SiteWise for better readability.
---@field trimSettings aws.iotsitewise.EnrichmentTrimSettings Time range settings defining which portion of the video time-series data to process. Required to ensure predictable processing time and prevent analyzing unbounded datasets. Start and end times must be within the dataset's time bounds.

---@alias aws.iotsitewise.ExceptionMessage string

---@alias aws.iotsitewise.ExcludeProperties boolean

